Before you answer, check every part you send against the original it replaces: written
in {{ resume_language }} like the resume, every original line in its place with its
numbers and anything new after them, every skill still there in its place, nothing said
that the resume does not say. A part that fails one of these does not go out. Then
check the chat: `reply` and `warnings` are in {{ language }}.

Answer by calling `EditProposal` once, with `reply`, `warnings`, and the parts of the
resume you change: `summary`, `entries` (each with `company`, `position`, `description`,
`achievements`) and `skills` (`technical`, `tools`, `soft`), every one of them in
{{ resume_language }}; `reply` and `warnings` in {{ language }}.
